{
  "_doc": [
    "What 'working' means for each tool, used by scripts/functional-suite.js.",
    "",
    "Defaults are applied by the driver: a tool taking application/pdf gets",
    "text.pdf, an image tool gets photo.jpg, and the assertion is that a",
    "non-empty file of the right type came back. Entries here override that",
    "with the semantics that actually matter — that redaction removes the",
    "text rather than covering it, that the EXIF stripper really drops GPS,",
    "that encryption rejects a wrong password.",
    "",
    "mode: 'download' (default) captures the file the tool produces.",
    "      'live' reads the panel's DOM output for tools that have no",
    "      download button (Base64, Unit Converter, and similar).",
    "      'skip' with a reason for tools that cannot run headless.",
    "",
    "assert: name of a checker in scripts/validate-output.py.",
    "input:  fixture filename, or a list. A list against two separate",
    "        single-file inputs is spread one fixture per input.",
    "fill:   [[selector, value], ...] applied after the file, before the action.",
    "click_first: selectors clicked before input — mode tabs and the like.",
    "action: selector of the button to press, when the last primary button",
    "        is not the one meant (Encode vs Decode).",
    "gestures: [{type:'draw'|'drag'|'tap', target, ...}] for tools that need",
    "        a signature stroke, a redaction rectangle, or a placement tap.",
    "        Fractions are relative to the target's bounding box."
  ],
